---

# 1. Document Purpose

This Functional Requirements Document defines the functional behavior, system capabilities, data interactions, validation requirements, and expected outcomes of the HR360 Human Resource Management & Analytics System.

The document translates the business requirements defined in the HR360 Business Requirements Document (BRD) into system-level functional requirements that can be implemented, tested, traced, and accepted.

The FRD serves as a baseline reference for:

* Application development
* REST API implementation
* Database integration
* Frontend development
* Functional testing
* User Acceptance Testing (UAT)
* Requirements traceability
* Analytics and Power BI integration

---

# 2. Scope

The HR360 system covers the following functional areas:

1. Employee Management
2. Department Management
3. Job Role Management
4. Workforce Status Management
5. Attendance Management
6. Leave Management
7. Performance Management
8. Performance Improvement Plans
9. Training Management
10. Recruitment Management
11. Candidate Management
12. Job Application Management
13. Interview Management
14. Job Offer Management
15. HR Analytics and Reporting
16. REST API and PostgreSQL data services

The frontend application and Power BI dashboards will consume the backend services and analytics data defined within this functional architecture.

---

# 3. System Overview

HR360 is a centralized Human Resource Management and Analytics platform designed to provide structured management of employee information, workforce activities, employee development, recruitment processes, and HR analytics.

The system follows a layered architecture:

**Frontend Layer**
React + Vite user interface

↓

**Application Layer**
Node.js + Express.js REST APIs

↓

**Data Layer**
PostgreSQL database

↓

**Analytics Layer**
HR360 Analytics APIs + Power BI

The backend provides controlled access to employee and HR data through RESTful APIs.

---

# 4. Functional Architecture

The HR360 functional architecture consists of the following major components.

| Component               | Responsibility                                         |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| Employee Management     | Maintain employee master data and lifecycle            |
| Organization Management | Manage departments and job roles                       |
| Workforce Management    | Manage work statuses and active-status rules           |
| Attendance              | Record and retrieve attendance information             |
| Leave Management        | Manage leave types and employee leave requests         |
| Performance             | Manage performance reviews and ratings                 |
| PIP                     | Manage Performance Improvement Plans                   |
| Training                | Manage training programs and employee participation    |
| Recruitment             | Manage candidates, applications, interviews and offers |
| Analytics               | Provide HR KPIs and analytical datasets                |
| API Layer               | Provide REST-based system integration                  |
| Database                | Persist transactional HR information                   |
| BI Layer                | Support management reporting and Power BI              |

---

# 5. User Roles and Actors

## 5.1 HR Business Stakeholder / Product Owner

Responsible for business ownership, requirement validation, prioritization, and acceptance of business functionality.

## 5.2 HR Manager

Uses HR360 for employee management, leave, performance, training, recruitment oversight, and HR reporting.

## 5.3 Operations Manager

Uses workforce, attendance, work-status, and operational analytics functionality.

## 5.4 Finance Manager

Uses employee salary-related information and finance-related workforce status information.

## 5.5 Recruitment / Talent Acquisition Lead

Uses candidate, application, interview, and job-offer functionality.

## 5.6 Business Managers

Use workforce and analytics information for management reporting and decision support.

## 5.7 Business End Users

Use applicable HR360 functionality according to their assigned responsibilities.

## 5.8 Application Owner / Administrator

Responsible for application configuration, API availability, data integrity, and technical maintenance.

