# 8. Employee Management Functional Requirements

## FR-EMP-001 — Create Employee

The system shall allow authorized users to create a new employee record.

The employee record shall contain relevant employee master information including:

* Employee code
* First name
* Last name
* Email
* Phone
* Department
* Job role
* Work status
* Employment status
* Joining date
* Salary information
* Salary status

The system shall validate mandatory fields before creating the record.

The employee code shall be unique.

---

## FR-EMP-002 — Retrieve Employee Information

The system shall allow authorized users to retrieve employee information.

The employee response shall include relevant organizational and workforce information, including:

* Department
* Job role
* Work status
* Employment status
* Salary status
* Department-specific active status

---

## FR-EMP-003 — Update Employee Information

The system shall allow authorized users to update employee information.

The system shall validate updated values before persistence.

Updates shall preserve database integrity and applicable business rules.

---

## FR-EMP-004 — Employee Lifecycle Status

The system shall support employee lifecycle statuses including:

* CANDIDATE
* PROBATION
* EMPLOYED
* ON_LEAVE
* RESIGNED
* TERMINATED
* RETIRED

Authorized users shall be able to update an employee's lifecycle status through the employee status functionality.

---

## FR-EMP-005 — Department-Specific Active Status

The system shall calculate the employee's active status based on department-specific business rules.

### HR

An HR employee shall be considered active when:

`employment_status = EMPLOYED`

### Operations

An Operations employee shall be considered active when:

`work_status = WORKING OR ONLINE`

### Finance

A Finance employee shall be considered active when:

`salary_status = PAID`

Employees that do not satisfy their department-specific rule shall be returned as:

`NOT ACTIVE`

The system shall calculate this value dynamically rather than storing a universal active flag.

---

# 9. Department Management Requirements

## FR-DEPT-001 — Department Management

The system shall allow authorized users to:

* Create departments
* Retrieve departments
* Update departments
* Maintain department information

Department names shall be uniquely identifiable within the organization.

---

# 10. Job Role Management Requirements

## FR-ROLE-001 — Job Role Management

The system shall allow authorized users to:

* Create job roles
* Retrieve job roles
* Update job roles
* Associate job roles with organizational functions

Job roles shall be available for employee and recruitment processes.

---

# 11. Workforce Status Requirements

## FR-WORK-001 — Work Status Management

The system shall maintain approved workforce statuses.

Supported statuses include:

* WORKING
* ONLINE
* TRAINING
* ON_BENCH
* PIP
* ON_LEAVE
* OFFLINE
* REMOTE

Authorized users shall be able to maintain work-status master data.

---

## FR-WORK-002 — Workforce Status Integration

The system shall use employee work status as an input to applicable workforce business rules.

For Operations employees, WORKING and ONLINE shall contribute to the department-specific active-status calculation.

---

# 12. Attendance Management Requirements

## FR-ATT-001 — Record Attendance

The system shall allow authorized users to record employee attendance.

Attendance information shall include:

* Employee
* Attendance date
* Attendance status
* Check-in time
* Check-out time
* Working hours
* Remarks

Supported attendance statuses include:

* PRESENT
* ABSENT
* LATE
* HALF_DAY
* ON_LEAVE
* HOLIDAY

---

## FR-ATT-002 — Retrieve Attendance

The system shall allow authorized users to retrieve attendance records.

Attendance information shall be available for operational reporting and analytics.

---

## FR-ATT-003 — Working Hours

The system shall store working-hours information where applicable.

Working hours shall support attendance analytics and operational reporting.

---

# 13. Leave Management Requirements

## FR-LEAVE-001 — Leave Type Management

The system shall maintain configurable leave types and applicable leave entitlements.

---

## FR-LEAVE-002 — Submit Leave Request

The system shall allow an employee or authorized HR user to submit a leave request.

A leave request shall contain:

* Employee
* Leave type
* Start date
* End date
* Number of days
* Reason
* Request status

---

## FR-LEAVE-003 — Leave Approval

The system shall allow authorized users to approve or reject leave requests.

The system shall maintain the status of each leave request.

---

## FR-LEAVE-004 — Leave Reporting

The system shall provide leave information for HR and management reporting.

---

# 14. Performance Management Requirements

## FR-PERF-001 — Performance Review

The system shall allow authorized users to record employee performance reviews.

A performance review may include:

* Employee
* Review period
* Reviewer
* Performance rating
* Comments
* Review status

---

## FR-PERF-002 — Performance History

The system shall retain historical performance review information for employees.

Performance information shall be available for reporting and analytics.

---

# 15. Performance Improvement Plan Requirements

## FR-PIP-001 — Create PIP

The system shall allow authorized users to create a Performance Improvement Plan for an employee.

The PIP shall support:

* Employee
* Start date
* End date
* Performance objectives
* Review frequency
* PIP status
* Review notes

---

## FR-PIP-002 — Track PIP

The system shall allow authorized users to track PIP progress and status.

PIP information shall be available for management and HR review.
# 16. Training Management Requirements

## FR-TRAIN-001 — Training Program Management

The system shall allow authorized users to create, retrieve, and maintain training programs.

Training programs shall support information including:

* Training name
* Training description
* Training status
* Training dates
* Training provider
* Training capacity
* Applicable training details

Training program statuses shall support the HR360 training lifecycle.

---

## FR-TRAIN-002 — Employee Training Enrollment

The system shall allow authorized users to enroll employees into training programs.

The employee-training record shall maintain:

* Employee
* Training program
* Enrollment date
* Attendance status
* Completion date
* Score
* Certificate status
* Employee feedback

---

## FR-TRAIN-003 — Training Completion

The system shall allow authorized users to record training completion.

Training participation statuses shall include:

* ENROLLED
* ATTENDED
* COMPLETED
* DID_NOT_ATTEND
* CANCELLED

Where applicable, the system shall store completion score and certificate information.

---

## FR-TRAIN-004 — Training Analytics

The system shall provide training information for analytics, including:

* Total training programs
* Employee participation
* Completed training
* Enrolled training
* Training scores
* Average training score

---

# 17. Recruitment Management Requirements

## FR-REC-001 — Candidate Management

The system shall allow authorized recruitment users to create and maintain candidate records.

Candidate information shall include:

* Candidate code
* First name
* Last name
* Email
* Phone
* Resume information
* Experience
* Qualification
* Current company
* Current designation
* Candidate source
* Candidate status
* Applied date

Candidate codes and email addresses shall be uniquely maintained.

---

## FR-REC-002 — Candidate Status

The system shall support candidate pipeline statuses including:

* NEW
* SCREENING
* SHORTLISTED
* INTERVIEW
* OFFERED
* HIRED
* REJECTED
* WITHDRAWN

Authorized users shall be able to update candidate status.

---

## FR-REC-003 — Job Application Management

The system shall allow recruitment users to create and manage job applications.

Each application shall associate:

* Candidate
* Job role
* Application date
* Application status
* Recruiter
* Expected salary
* Notice period
* Recruiter notes

The system shall prevent duplicate applications for the same candidate and job role.

---

## FR-REC-004 — Application Status Management

The system shall support application statuses including:

* APPLIED
* SCREENING
* SHORTLISTED
* INTERVIEW
* OFFERED
* HIRED
* REJECTED
* WITHDRAWN

The system shall retain the current application status for recruitment tracking.

---

# 18. Interview Management Requirements

## FR-REC-005 — Schedule Interview

The system shall allow authorized recruitment users to schedule interviews against job applications.

Interview information shall include:

* Application
* Interviewer
* Interview round
* Interview type
* Scheduled date
* Scheduled time
* Interview status

---

## FR-REC-006 — Record Interview Outcome

The system shall allow authorized interviewers or recruitment users to record:

* Interview rating
* Feedback
* Result

Supported interview statuses shall include:

* SCHEDULED
* COMPLETED
* CANCELLED
* NO_SHOW

Interview results shall support:

* PASS
* FAIL
* PENDING

Interview ratings shall be maintained within the defined rating range.

---

# 19. Job Offer Management Requirements

## FR-REC-007 — Create Job Offer

The system shall allow authorized recruitment users to create a job offer against a job application.

An offer shall include:

* Application
* Offer date
* Joining date
* Offered salary
* Employment type
* Offer status
* Accepted date
* Rejection reason

---

## FR-REC-008 — Offer Status Management

The system shall support offer statuses including:

* DRAFT
* SENT
* ACCEPTED
* DECLINED
* EXPIRED
* CANCELLED

The system shall maintain offer status throughout the offer lifecycle.

---

## FR-REC-009 — Offer Validation

The system shall ensure that:

* Offered salary is greater than zero.
* Joining date cannot be earlier than the offer date.
* An application cannot have multiple job offers where the data model requires a unique offer relationship.
* Accepted date shall be recorded when an offer is accepted.

---

# 20. Recruitment-to-Employee Transition

## FR-REC-010 — Accepted Offer Transition

The target HR360 process shall support transition from an accepted job offer to an employee record.

The transition shall ensure that recruitment information and employee information remain traceable.

This capability is classified as **Target / Planned** where the automated transition has not yet been implemented in the current backend.

The future process shall avoid duplicate employee records and maintain the relationship between:

**Candidate → Application → Offer → Employee**

---

# 21. HR Analytics and Reporting Requirements

## FR-AN-001 — HR Overview Analytics

The system shall provide an HR analytics overview containing key workforce indicators.

The overview shall support information such as:

* Total employees
* Active employees according to applicable business rules
* Workforce distribution
* Employee lifecycle information
* Other configured HR KPIs

---

## FR-AN-002 — Department Analytics

The system shall provide department-level analytics.

The analytics shall support comparison of workforce information across departments, including:

* Employee counts
* Workforce status
* Department activity
* Applicable employee metrics

---

## FR-AN-003 — Attendance Analytics

The system shall provide attendance analytics based on recorded attendance data.

Analytics shall support attendance statuses including:

* PRESENT
* ABSENT
* LATE
* HALF_DAY
* ON_LEAVE
* HOLIDAY

---

## FR-AN-004 — Leave Analytics

The system shall provide leave-related analytics, including leave request information and applicable leave statuses.

---

## FR-AN-005 — Performance Analytics

The system shall provide performance-related analytics using employee performance review information.

Performance analytics may include:

* Review counts
* Performance ratings
* Average performance rating
* Employee performance distribution

---

## FR-AN-006 — Training Analytics

The system shall provide training analytics using employee training records.

Training analytics shall support:

* Total training records
* Completed training
* Enrolled training
* Employee participation
* Average training score

---

## FR-AN-007 — Recruitment Analytics

The system shall provide recruitment analytics using candidate, application, interview, and job-offer information.

Recruitment analytics shall support pipeline visibility across recruitment stages.

---

# 22. API Functional Requirements

## FR-API-001 — REST API Services

The system shall expose REST APIs for supported HR360 modules.

The API layer shall provide appropriate operations for:

* Retrieval
* Creation
* Update
* Status changes
* Module-specific operations

The primary API areas are:

| Module              | Base Endpoint              |
| ------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Employees           | `/api/employees`           |
| Departments         | `/api/departments`         |
| Job Roles           | `/api/job-roles`           |
| Work Statuses       | `/api/work-statuses`       |
| Attendance          | `/api/attendance`          |
| Leave Types         | `/api/leave-types`         |
| Leave Requests      | `/api/leave-requests`      |
| Performance Reviews | `/api/performance-reviews` |
| PIPs                | `/api/pips`                |
| Training Programs   | `/api/training-programs`   |
| Employee Training   | `/api/employee-training`   |
| Candidates          | `/api/candidates`          |
| Job Applications    | `/api/job-applications`    |
| Interviews          | `/api/interviews`          |
| Job Offers          | `/api/job-offers`          |
| Analytics           | `/api/analytics`           |

---

## FR-API-002 — API Validation

The system shall validate incoming API requests before database persistence.

Validation shall include:

* Mandatory fields
* Valid identifiers
* Valid status values
* Valid numeric values
* Valid dates
* Foreign-key relationships
* Business-rule constraints

---

## FR-API-003 — API Error Handling

The API shall return appropriate HTTP status codes and structured error responses.

The system shall not expose database credentials, environment variables, or other sensitive configuration information in API responses.

---

# 23. Database Functional Requirements

## FR-DB-001 — PostgreSQL Persistence

The HR360 backend shall use PostgreSQL as the primary transactional database.

The database shall persist HR360 master, transactional, recruitment, performance, training, and analytics-related information.

---

## FR-DB-002 — Referential Integrity

The system shall maintain relationships between related entities using appropriate database constraints.

Examples include:

* Employee → Department
* Employee → Job Role
* Employee → Work Status
* Attendance → Employee
* Leave Request → Employee
* Performance Review → Employee
* PIP → Employee
* Employee Training → Employee
* Employee Training → Training Program
* Application → Candidate
* Application → Job Role
* Interview → Application
* Job Offer → Application

---

## FR-DB-003 — Data Validation

Database constraints shall be used where appropriate to protect data integrity.

Examples include:

* Unique employee codes
* Unique candidate codes
* Unique email addresses where applicable
* Valid status values
* Positive salary values
* Valid ratings
* Valid date relationships

---

# 24. Validation and Business Rule Integration

The application shall apply the HR360 Business Rules Catalogue during relevant transactions.

The most significant workforce rule is the department-specific active-status calculation.

| Department        | Active Condition                                                              |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| HR                | `employment_status = EMPLOYED`                                                |
| Operations        | `work_status IN (WORKING, ONLINE)`                                            |
| Finance           | `salary_status = PAID`                                                        |
| Other Departments | Not automatically classified as active by the three department-specific rules |

The system shall return the derived value:

`ACTIVE`

or

`NOT ACTIVE`

where applicable.

The system shall not introduce a universal stored `active` field that overrides the department-specific business rules.

---

# 25. Security Requirements

## FR-SEC-001 — Credential Protection

Database credentials and environment-specific secrets shall be stored outside source-code files.

The `.env` file shall not be committed to Git.

---

## FR-SEC-002 — Sensitive Data Protection

The system shall not expose:

* Database passwords
* API secrets
* Authentication tokens
* Environment configuration secrets

through application responses or documentation.

---

## FR-SEC-003 — Controlled Access

Future frontend and authentication layers shall restrict sensitive HR operations according to user roles and permissions.

---

# 26. Non-Functional Requirements

## NFR-001 — Performance

The system should provide responsive API operations for normal HR360 transactional workloads.

## NFR-002 — Availability

The backend application and PostgreSQL database should be available during defined business operating periods.

## NFR-003 — Scalability

The architecture should support future expansion of employee volume, HR modules, analytics, and frontend functionality.

## NFR-004 — Maintainability

The application shall use modular backend routes and maintain separation between:

* Server configuration
* Database connectivity
* API routes
* Business logic
* Analytics services

## NFR-005 — Data Integrity

The system shall preserve referential integrity and validate data before persistence.

## NFR-006 — Usability

The planned frontend shall provide clear navigation, consistent forms, understandable validation messages, and role-appropriate dashboards.

## NFR-007 — Auditability

Important HR transactions should maintain appropriate timestamps and status information to support operational traceability.

---

# 27. Business Rules Integration

The following major business-rule categories shall be integrated with the functional requirements:

| Rule Area                | Functional Impact                                       |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| Employee Lifecycle       | Controls employee employment status                     |
| Department Active Status | Determines department-specific activity                 |
| Work Status              | Supports workforce operational status                   |
| Attendance               | Controls attendance classification                      |
| Leave                    | Controls leave request processing                       |
| Performance              | Supports review and rating processes                    |
| PIP                      | Supports performance improvement tracking               |
| Training                 | Controls training participation lifecycle               |
| Recruitment              | Controls candidate and application pipeline             |
| Interviews               | Controls interview status and outcomes                  |
| Job Offers               | Controls offer lifecycle                                |
| Analytics                | Converts transactional data into management information |

---

